<!--
  TipTapAsyncModelRaceDemo.rozie — behavioral cell for the async-construction
  write race (quick 260926, audit follow-up to quick 260925-r41's `ready`
  event).

  `maxLength` forces the CharacterCount extension to load with a dynamic
  import() before the Editor is constructed (see TipTap.rozie's $onMount).
  This demo's OWN $onMount defers the child's exposed `setContent()` call by
  ONE microtask (`queueMicrotask`) — strictly before the child's
  maxLength-triggered import() can possibly settle (a real dynamic import()
  always takes at least a task, not just a microtask, to resolve), but
  strictly AFTER every onMount callback queued in the CURRENT synchronous
  render pass has run. That second property matters: Solid's onMount queue is
  REGISTRATION order, not DOM-tree order — a bare `$onMount(() =>
  $refs.ed.setContent(...))` (registered textually above the `<TipTap>`, hence
  queued BEFORE it) would fire before the child ever assigns its ref, silently
  no-op'ing the whole reproduction on Solid only. The microtask deferral makes
  the sequencing deterministic and target-agnostic without depending on
  Playwright click timing (which raced ready in local dev/preview — the
  dynamic import can resolve faster than a real click round-trip).

  Before the fix, `setContent` returned early on `!editor` and silently
  dropped the write; the eventual `ready` payload's `getHTML()` still showed
  the ORIGINAL seed. After the fix, the write updates the model even
  pre-construction, so `construct()` (which reads the html model fresh) picks
  it up and the final content reflects the injected value.

  Angular's component ref resolves to the host element, not the exposed
  handle (the documented per-target idiom — same gate as tiptap.spec.ts), so
  `$refs.ed?.setContent?.()` is a harmless no-op there; the spec excludes
  Angular from the assertion.
-->

<rozie name="TipTapAsyncModelRaceDemo">

<components>
{
  TipTap: '../../packages/ui/tiptap/src/TipTap.rozie',
}
</components>

<data>
{
  html: '<p>original seed</p>',
  finalHtml: '(pending)',
}
</data>

<script>
const onReady = (editor) => {
  $data.finalHtml = editor && typeof editor.getHTML === 'function' ? editor.getHTML() : '(no editor)'
}

$onMount(() => {
  queueMicrotask(() => {
    $refs.ed?.setContent?.('<p>INJECTED BEFORE READY</p>')
  })
})
</script>

<template>
<div class="tiptap-race-demo">
  <h3>TipTap — async model race</h3>
  <div data-testid="editor"><TipTap ref="ed" r-model:html="$data.html" :maxLength="50" @ready="onReady" /></div>
  <pre data-testid="final-html">{{ $data.finalHtml }}</pre>
</div>
</template>

<style>
.tiptap-race-demo {
  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
  color: #1a1a1a;
  padding: 1rem;
  max-width: 720px;
}
.tiptap-race-demo h3 { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-size: 1rem; }
</style>

</rozie>
